<title>USA: IWC Q4 hurt by higher oper expenses.</title>
<headline>IWC Q4 hurt by higher oper expenses.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS, Ind. 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>IWC Resources Corp attributed its lower fourth-quarter earnings to increased operating expenses during the period resulting from its pending merger with NIPSCO Industries Inc.</p>
<p>Other factors included a reduction in land sales in 1996 compared to 1995 and an increase in operating expenses in the utility-regulated services segment resulting from continued expansion of business.</p>
<p>The utility holding company reported fourth-quarter earnings of $0.09 a share, down from $0.41 in the same 1995 period. Revenues fell to $44.5 million from $45.8 million.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
</text>
